{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789232758,"nonce":"uIrQPXxtRq7gLcH5Mg/J+hBmElA=","title":"The main Cranelift path drops Realloc, Memcpy, Memmove and Memset calls silently","message":"`compile_module`'s instruction loop handles a `Call` to an intrinsic\nwith a match whose fallback is `continue`: an intrinsic the arm list\ndoes not name emits nothing and leaves its result out of the value\nmap, so the next instruction that uses the result panics with \"no\nentry found for key\" deep in the backend. `Realloc`, `Memcpy`,\n`Memmove` and `Memset` are all missing there while the secondary\ncompile path (the one used for OSR entry functions) implements them.\n\nFix: implement the four in the main path, sharing the `call_realloc` /\n`call_memcpy` helpers, and make the fallback an error naming the\nintrinsic instead of a `continue`.","files":null}]}